    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d578">

                <pb facs="0650" n="1328" xml:id="pg1328"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Dayton.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 434.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-11-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 25, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of October
                    29, (No. 371,) which gives an account of the entrance of the pirate Georgia into
                    Cherbourg, and of your proceedings therein. The President’s views of these
                    events have been made known in a previous communication.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> L. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dayton</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c.,
                            &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
